{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>When shall I provide for my own house</b> — Now, they do not work for my needs, but rather my children, and I need to work alongside them to sustain them, and this is also the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 30:30). But we do not find that Jacob had any flocks, nor that his small sons tended them, for the eldest among them was six years old or less, since Laban — it stands to reason that he had sons younger than Rachel before Jacob came, and now they are fit to tend the flocks. And perhaps he was referring to his wives and his servants, that they would work for him in labor. But none of this is correct. Rather, the meaning of \"When shall I provide also for my own house\" is: When shall I also provide for my own house, just as I have provided also for your house. And likewise, \"And he loved also Rachel, more than Leah\" (Genesis 29:30) — and he loved Rachel more than Leah; and likewise, \"I would have slain also you\" (Numbers 22:33) — I would have slain you as well; and there are many like these."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:37:16.292906569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}